<title>UK: Yorkshire Water H1 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire Water H1 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		50.0		   vs 47.1</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 10.2		   vs 9.1</p>
<p> Pretax		     109.4		  vs 99.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   310.9		  vs 292.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 105 to 110 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 118.7		  vs 103.5</p>
<p> Interest payable	 8.3		    vs 6.3</p>
<p> Tax			  8.8		    vs 3.9</p>
<p> Net taxed		  100.6		  vs 95.6</p>
<p> Attributable	     100.4		  vs 95.4</p>
<p> Pay date		   Feb 24, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 17</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said its interim payout was in line with its aim to pay six to eight percent real dividend increases annually to the year 2000.</p>
<p>The company reiterated that it was anxious to improve its balance sheet by the introduction of higher levels of debt before the end of the current financial year.</p>
<p>&quot;A range of options is actively being pursued with a view to maximising shareholder value,&quot; the utility said in its statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
